;; rules/booklogic/queries.edn — Datalog queries over the atomspace.
;;
;; FORM SYNTAX:
;;   (defquery :Q001-name
;;     :backend :cozo
;;     :body (datalog-clauses ...))
;;
;; Queries run against Cozo (Datalog backend). The body is a sequence of
;; Cozo-style rules; the verifier's kg.rs translates them and emits
;; matched-claim ids alongside the verdict.
;;
;; CURRENT STATUS: STUB. defquery forms compile via codegen_kg.py but
;; the result is not consumed in `npm run build` by default. Tier 3 of
;; the framework roadmap promotes Cozo from stub-builder to wired path.
;; See SUPPORT_MATRIX.md.
;;
;; EXAMPLE (commented out — uncomment and edit for your domain):
;; (defquery :Q001-orphan-claims
;;   :backend :cozo
;;   :body  [(orphan ?c) :- (:claim ?c)
;;                          (not (:supports-chapter ?c _))])
;;
;; COMMON SILENT FAILURES:
;;   - :backend :z3 → silently dropped (defquery is Cozo-only by design).
;;   - referencing an undeclared predicate in the body → Cozo throws
;;     at query-execution time, not at compile time.
;;
{:forms []}
